  "_purpose": "Compliance rules for auditing our own content before publishing. A hard block means: remove or rewrite that content, there is no valid workaround. These lists are editable data, not code.",
  "engine": {
    "normalization": "Lowercase, diacritics folded (á→a, ü→u, ł→l, ñ→n), ß→ss, and every non-letter or non-digit collapsed to a single space. The terms in this table are already written in normalized, folded form. matchedTerms.index always points at the ORIGINAL text: the engine keeps a map from normalized positions back to the original.",
    "matchModes": {
      "word": "An exact run of consecutive tokens over the normalized text, so multi-token phrases like 'waffen ss' work. Required for short terms (4 characters or fewer) and acronyms: after folding ß to ss, 'ss' sits inside strasse, wasser and besser, so substring would fire false positives.",
      "substring": "A substring of the normalized text. Only for long terms that appear inside German compounds (hakenkreuzfahne, hitlergrusses)."
    },
    "caseGuard": "Uppercase guard: for single-token word rules whose term is 4 characters or fewer (ss, sa, hj, kz), a match only counts when the ORIGINAL slice is fully uppercase. 'SA marschierte' matches; 'Sa. geschlossen' (Saturday) does not. On by default; a rule can opt out with \"caseGuard\": false (bdm, for instance, does not collide with ordinary German). Does not apply to multi-token phrases or to substring rules."
  },
